2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1033) '`MIT*` is MIT with an employer disclaimer. Decimation is listed apart from retopology because the two answer different questions: retopology rebuilds the edge flow, decimation removes elements from the flow that is there, and an avatar losing triangles without losing its silhouette wants the second. PMP and Geogram are vendored in &{repo("entities-godot")} on `feat/cassie`; RFD66606-1029 records the licenses as read from those copies and why blend shape transfer, not triangle removal, is the hard half.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1033  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1033) 'Each one is packaged as its own model image, per RFD66606-1036.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1033  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1033) 'How they scale
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1033  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1033) 'These algorithms hold no weights. Their memory scales with the mesh, and not with a parameter count. A capacity plan must therefore use the vertex budget, and not a bf16 figure.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1033  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1033) 'src/library/aiModelsCatalog.js caps the mesh at 210,000 vertices. The constant is `API_MAX_MESH_VERTICES`, and it matches the API upload cap.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1033  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-1033) 'A license note
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1033  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1033) 'quadwild_retopology uses the GPL-3 license, which RFD66606-1028 excludes. Instant Meshes is the permissive replacement, and RFD66606-1029 records the other options.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1033  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1033) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1033  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1033) 'The two kinds scale in different ways.
